<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Linda Hale, VP Customer Operations. Not technical. Emailed. Wants one thing
  she can forward to a customer, and whether the date will hold. When the date
  slips again to Wednesday she has to walk back what she told the customer.
-->
<aiml>
  <category><pattern>*</pattern><template>
    <think>
      <set var="date"><srai>XDATE <star/></srai></set>
      <set var="tech"><srai>XTECH <star/></srai></set>
      <set var="firm"><srai>XFIRM <star/></srai></set>
      <set var="hedge"><srai>XHEDGE <star/></srai></set>
      <set var="wed"><srai>XWED <star/></srai></set>
    </think>
    <condition>
      <li name="done2" value="yes"></li>
      <li name="stage" value="correcting">
        <think><set name="done2">yes</set></think>
        <condition>
          <li var="hedge" value="yes">Thank you. I'll send that on and keep it tentative this time.<br/><br/>Linda</li>
          <li>Thanks, I'll send that on.<br/><br/>Linda</li>
        </condition>
      </li>
      <li var="wed" value="yes">
        <think><set name="stage">correcting</set></think>
        <condition>
          <li name="done" value="yes">Oh no. I already told Harrow &amp; Finch it was Monday. What happened? I need a couple of sentences I can send them to correct it -- they're planning their month-end close around this.<br/><br/>Linda</li>
          <li>Thanks. So it's Wednesday the 30th now? Can I give the customer that date?<br/><br/>Linda</li>
        </condition>
      </li>
      <li name="done" value="yes"></li>
      <li name="asked_firm" value="yes">
        <think><set name="done">yes</set></think>
        <condition>
          <li var="hedge" value="yes">Understood. I'll tell them early next week and confirm once it's actually out.<br/><br/>Thanks,<br/>Linda</li>
          <li var="firm" value="yes">Great, I'll let Harrow &amp; Finch know it's Monday.<br/><br/>Thanks!<br/>Linda</li>
          <li>OK, thanks. I'll pass along Monday.<br/><br/>Linda</li>
        </condition>
      </li>
      <li var="tech" value="yes">
        <condition var="date">
          <li value="yes"><think><set name="asked_firm">yes</set></think>Thanks for the detail. I'll be honest, most of the technical part is over my head. Is Monday firm enough that I can give it to the customer, or should I hedge?<br/><br/>Linda</li>
          <li><random><li>Thanks. I'm afraid I don't follow the technical part. Is it shipping this week or not, and if not, when?<br/><br/>Linda</li><li>Sorry, most of that is beyond me. Is it this week or not, and if not, when?<br/><br/>Linda</li><li>Thanks, but I'm not technical. Can you just tell me whether it ships this week, and if not, the date?<br/><br/>Linda</li></random></li>
        </condition>
      </li>
      <li var="date" value="yes"><think><set name="asked_firm">yes</set></think>Perfect, thank you. Is Monday firm, or should I hedge with the customer?<br/><br/>Linda</li>
      <li><random><li>Thanks. Do you have a date I can pass along?<br/><br/>Linda</li><li>Thanks for coming back to me. Is there a date I can give them?<br/><br/>Linda</li><li>Appreciated. Do we have a date yet? That's what they're really after.<br/><br/>Linda</li></random></li>
    </condition>
  </template></category>

  <category><pattern>XFIRM # FIRM #</pattern><template>yes</template></category>
  <category><pattern>XFIRM # CONFIDENT #</pattern><template>yes</template></category>
  <category><pattern>XFIRM # ON TRACK #</pattern><template>yes</template></category>
  <category><pattern>XFIRM # COMMIT #</pattern><template>yes</template></category>
  <category><pattern>XFIRM # YES #</pattern><template>yes</template></category>
  <category><pattern>XFIRM *</pattern><template>no</template></category>
  <category><pattern>XFIRM</pattern><template>no</template></category>

  <category><pattern>XHEDGE # HEDGE #</pattern><template>yes</template></category>
  <category><pattern>XHEDGE # TENTATIVE #</pattern><template>yes</template></category>
  <category><pattern>XHEDGE # EARLY NEXT WEEK #</pattern><template>yes</template></category>
  <category><pattern>XHEDGE # CAN T PROMISE #</pattern><template>yes</template></category>
  <category><pattern>XHEDGE # CANNOT PROMISE #</pattern><template>yes</template></category>
  <category><pattern>XHEDGE # NOT FIRM #</pattern><template>yes</template></category>
  <category><pattern>XHEDGE # NOT GUARANTEED #</pattern><template>yes</template></category>
  <category><pattern>XHEDGE # ESTIMATE #</pattern><template>yes</template></category>
  <category><pattern>XHEDGE *</pattern><template>no</template></category>
  <category><pattern>XHEDGE</pattern><template>no</template></category>
</aiml>
